{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Image Fundamentals \u2014 Pixels, Channels, Color Spaces Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Load an image and inspect its shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Use Pillow to load any JPEG or PNG, convert to NumPy, and print what you got. For a deterministic example that runs offline, synthesize one."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from PIL import Image"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def synthetic_rgb(h=128, w=192, seed=0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    yy, xx = np.meshgrid(np.linspace(0, 1, h), np.linspace(0, 1, w), indexing=\"ij\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    r = (np.sin(xx * 6) * 0.5 + 0.5) * 255"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    g = yy * 255"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    b = (1 - yy) * xx * 255"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rgb = np.stack([r, g, b], axis=-1) + rng.normal(0, 6, (h, w, 3))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return np.clip(rgb, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "arr = synthetic_rgb()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Or load from disk:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# arr = np.asarray(Image.open(\"your_image.jpg\").convert(\"RGB\"))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"type:   {type(arr).__name__}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"dtype:  {arr.dtype}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"shape:  {arr.shape}     # (H, W, C)\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"min:    {arr.min()}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"max:    {arr.max()}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"pixel at (0, 0): {arr[0, 0]}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Expected output: `shape: (H, W, 3)`, `dtype: uint8`, range `[0, 255]`. That is the canonical on-disk representation whether the bytes came from a camera, a JPEG decoder, or a synthetic generator."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Split channels and re-order layout"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Pull out R, G, B separately, then convert from HWC to CHW for PyTorch."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "R = arr[:, :, 0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "G = arr[:, :, 1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "B = arr[:, :, 2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"R shape: {R.shape}, mean: {R.mean():.1f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"G shape: {G.shape}, mean: {G.mean():.1f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"B shape: {B.shape}, mean: {B.mean():.1f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "arr_chw = arr.transpose(2, 0, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"\\nHWC shape: {arr.shape}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"CHW shape: {arr_chw.shape}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Three grayscale planes, one per channel. CHW just reorders the axes; no data copy is strictly required when the memory layout allows it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Grayscale and HSV conversions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Weighted-sum grayscale, then a manual RGB-to-HSV."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def rgb_to_grayscale(rgb):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    weights = np.array([0.299, 0.587, 0.114], dtype=np.float32)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return (rgb.astype(np.float32) @ weights).astype(np.uint8)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def rgb_to_hsv(rgb):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rgb_f = rgb.astype(np.float32) / 255.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    r, g, b = rgb_f[..., 0], rgb_f[..., 1], rgb_f[..., 2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    cmax = np.max(rgb_f, axis=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    cmin = np.min(rgb_f, axis=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    delta = cmax - cmin"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    h = np.zeros_like(cmax)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mask = delta > 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rmax = mask & (cmax == r)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    gmax = mask & (cmax == g)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    bmax = mask & (cmax == b)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    h[rmax] = ((g[rmax] - b[rmax]) / delta[rmax]) % 6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    h[gmax] = ((b[gmax] - r[gmax]) / delta[gmax]) + 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    h[bmax] = ((r[bmax] - g[bmax]) / delta[bmax]) + 4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    h = h * 60.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    s = np.where(cmax > 0, delta / cmax, 0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    v = cmax"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return np.stack([h, s, v], axis=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "gray = rgb_to_grayscale(arr)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "hsv = rgb_to_hsv(arr)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"gray shape: {gray.shape}, range: [{gray.min()}, {gray.max()}]\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"hsv   shape: {hsv.shape}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"hue range: [{hsv[..., 0].min():.1f}, {hsv[..., 0].max():.1f}] degrees\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"sat range: [{hsv[..., 1].min():.2f}, {hsv[..., 1].max():.2f}]\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"val range: [{hsv[..., 2].min():.2f}, {hsv[..., 2].max():.2f}]\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Hue comes out in degrees, saturation and value in [0, 1]. That matches the OpenCV `hsv_full` convention."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Normalize, standardize, and reverse it"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Go from raw bytes to the exact tensor a pretrained ImageNet model expects, then back."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "mean = np.array([0.485, 0.456, 0.406], dtype=np.float32)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "std = np.array([0.229, 0.224, 0.225], dtype=np.float32)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def preprocess_imagenet(rgb_uint8):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = rgb_uint8.astype(np.float32) / 255.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = (x - mean) / std"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = x.transpose(2, 0, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def deprocess_imagenet(chw_float32):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = chw_float32.transpose(1, 2, 0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = x * std + mean"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = np.clip(x * 255.0, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "x = preprocess_imagenet(arr)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"preprocessed shape: {x.shape}     # (C, H, W)\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"preprocessed dtype: {x.dtype}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"preprocessed mean per channel:  {x.mean(axis=(1, 2)).round(3)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"preprocessed std  per channel:  {x.std(axis=(1, 2)).round(3)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "roundtrip = deprocess_imagenet(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "max_diff = np.abs(roundtrip.astype(int) - arr.astype(int)).max()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"roundtrip max pixel diff: {max_diff}    # should be 0 or 1\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Per-channel mean should be close to zero, std close to one. The preprocess/deprocess pair is exactly what every torchvision `transforms.Normalize` call is doing under the hood."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Resize with three interpolation methods"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Compare nearest, bilinear, and bicubic on an upscale so the difference is visible."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "target = (arr.shape[0] * 3, arr.shape[1] * 3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "nearest = np.asarray(Image.fromarray(arr).resize(target[::-1], Image.NEAREST))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "bilinear = np.asarray(Image.fromarray(arr).resize(target[::-1], Image.BILINEAR))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "bicubic = np.asarray(Image.fromarray(arr).resize(target[::-1], Image.BICUBIC))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def local_roughness(x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    gy = np.diff(x.astype(float), axis=0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    gx = np.diff(x.astype(float), axis=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return float(np.abs(gy).mean() + np.abs(gx).mean())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for name, out in [(\"nearest\", nearest), (\"bilinear\", bilinear), (\"bicubic\", bicubic)]:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"{name:>8}  shape={out.shape}  roughness={local_roughness(out):6.2f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Nearest scores highest on roughness because it keeps hard edges. Bilinear is the smoothest. Bicubic sits in between, preserving perceived sharpness without the stair-step artifacts."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **(Easy)** Load a JPEG with OpenCV (`cv2.imread`) and with Pillow. Print both shapes and the pixel at `(0, 0)`. Explain the channel-order difference, then write a one-line conversion that makes the OpenCV array identical to the Pillow one.\n2. **(Medium)** Write `standardize(img, mean, std)` and its inverse that together pass a `roundtrip_max_diff <= 1` test on any uint8 image. Your functions must work on a single image in HWC and on a batch in NCHW with the same call.\n3. **(Hard)** Take a 3-channel ImageNet-standardized tensor and run it through a 1x1 conv that learns a weighted mixture of RGB into a single grayscale channel. Initialize the weights to `[0.299, 0.587, 0.114]`, freeze them, and verify the output matches your manual `rgb_to_grayscale` to within floating-point error. What other classical color-space transforms can be written as 1x1 convolutions?"
      ]
    }
  ],
